 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338178 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f52f84db-f262-57d1-9c5e-5a630266362b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338234 #edb/ref 1080 "⟨0,-2,1⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338234 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338234 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fb04c736-1e93-5392-937a-e6b52b89f395" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338374 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425107 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338374 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338374 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425110 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338374 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338374 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425114 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338374 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338374 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338374 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425110 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338374 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "335b522d-b8a5-5ac7-8b9d-2985076f5c17" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338414 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338414 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336339 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338414 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336692 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338414 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336814 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338414 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186338234 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338414 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338414 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338414 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186336053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338414 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4ee8ed97-cdf9-56b8-9f86-2a9258c8b74b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338458 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336234 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338458 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338458 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338458 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338458 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186338127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338458 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338458 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338458 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186336573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338458 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "67c2ebb0-7f04-5390-9b3f-6c5b9ac02ee1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338478 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336530 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338478 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338478 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338478 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186338046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338478 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186338178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338478 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338478 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338478 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186338046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338478 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7598b8df-f496-507a-9973-2189f2324d0b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338568 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336198 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338568 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336624 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338568 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186336849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338568 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338568 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338568 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338568 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338568 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186336849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338568 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9f6508aa-26cc-5e67-a21e-e797c69eabff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338912 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338912 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71198" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338912 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338912 #edb/ref 1071 "A surface $S$ is defined by $z=f(x,y).$ The curve $C$ is the intersection of $S$ with the plane $x=2.$ Given that the point $P$ with $y$-coordinate $1$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=3{x}^{2}y-6x{y}^{2}$, find the slope of the tangent to $C$ at $P.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338912 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6efe9457-81ed-5961-99c6-f2de702a7e78" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338912 #edb/ref 1074 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point where $y=1$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(2,1).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(2,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(2,1) & =3(2)^{2}(1)-6(2)(1)^{2} \\\\  & =12-12 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338917 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338458 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338917 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71218" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338917 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338917 #edb/ref 1071 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=1.$ Given that the point $P(0,1,2)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338917 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ceda561f-8269-5197-b05a-efc41af9a9a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338917 #edb/ref 1074 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(0,1,2)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(0,1)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(0,1)} & =(0)^{2}+(1)^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0+1) \\\\  & =1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(0,1)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(0,1)}(x-0) \\\\ z-2 & =1(x) \\\\ z & =x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(0,1,2)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=1 \\\\ z &=x+2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186338918 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338414 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338918 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71220" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338918 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338918 #edb/ref 1071 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=-2.$ Given that the point $P(-2,-6,1)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=\\frac{y-x}{\\sqrt{x(y+x)}}$, which of the following gives a tangent vector to $C$ at $P?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338918 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2d6bbe53-bb73-5d24-b77f-7c5fef3fe5bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338918 #edb/ref 1074 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $x=-2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(-2,-6).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(-2,-6):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(-2,-6) & =\\frac{-6-(-2)}{\\sqrt{(-2)(-6+(-2))}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{\\sqrt{16}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{4} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(-2,-6) & ={f}_{y}(-2,-6)(y-(-6)) \\\\ z-1 & =-1(y+6) \\\\ z-1 & =-y-6 \\\\ z & =-y-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-2,-6,1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2 \\\\ z &=-y-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=-2,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=-y-5$ (or $y+z+5=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,1,1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $⟨0,-1,1⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186338919 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338568 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338919 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71221" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338919 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338919 #edb/ref 1071 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=1.$ Given that the point $P(-1,1,-1)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=3{e}^{x+y}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|xy|$, which of the following gives a tangent vector to $C$ at $P?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338919 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8b7dd45b-b8d1-582b-9fbf-c50179d63d9b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338919 #edb/ref 1074 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $y=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(-1,1).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ at $(-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(-1,1) & =3{e}^{-1+1}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(-1)\\cdot 1| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\  & =3-0 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(-1,1) & ={f}_{x}(-1,1)(x-(-1)) \\\\ z-(-1) & =3(x+1) \\\\ z+1 & =3x+3 \\\\ z & =3x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-1,1,-1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=1 \\\\ z &=3x+2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $y=1,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,1,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=3x+2$ (or $3x-z+2=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨3,0,-1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨0,1,0⟩\\times ⟨3,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i-3\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $⟨-1,0,-3⟩$ is parallel to the tangent line, then $-⟨-1,0,-3⟩=⟨1,0,3⟩$ is also parallel to it." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186385351 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186514935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385351 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385351 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385351 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385351 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186515321 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385351 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385351 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385351 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186515186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186385351 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ec17033d-7e32-53b3-b00f-f4c5e370a468" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406791 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406791 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406791 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406791 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406791 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #e