045417] [17592186425117 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425117 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425117 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425117 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425103 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425117 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186425104 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425117 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425117 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425117 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186425098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425117 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9d7802a6-4174-5690-9124-8f551b3466e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425120 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186425115 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425120 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71226" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425120 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425120 #edb/ref 1071 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=5.$ Given that the point $P(4,5,-2)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=\\frac{\\sqrt{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}}{2x-y}$, which of the following gives a tangent vector to $C$ at $P?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425120 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d880e565-bd50-5672-98e1-45142968e59d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425120 #edb/ref 1074 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $y=5.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(4,5).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ at $(4,5):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(4,5) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{(5)^{2}-(4)^{2}}}{2(4)-(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{9}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(4,5) & ={f}_{x}(4,5)(x-4) \\\\ z-(-2) & =1(x-4) \\\\ z+2 & =x-4 \\\\ z & =x-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(4,5,-2)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=5 \\\\ z &=x-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $y=5,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,1,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=x-6$ (or $x-z-6=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,0,-1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨0,1,0⟩\\times ⟨1,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $-i-k$ is parallel to the tangent line, then $-(-i-k)=i+k$ is also parallel to it." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186425121 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0dfd5f35-4d13-5e8b-b12c-5286da4ef943" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425121 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186268885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425122 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186425125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425122 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "37de0ec1-dde9-55e5-b218-6452fee1d909" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425122 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186425118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425123 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186425124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425123 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a385dd67-f4d9-5c4e-9dcb-07bacb547fb1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425123 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186425120 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425124 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186425121 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425124 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a445cd29-271b-5b63-aa35-8be905e25a57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425124 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186425119 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425125 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186425123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425125 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dc115997-e200-5133-98f2-30e70726764f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425125 #e